# Fallow quality gates

When `{{packageManager}} run check:fallow` fails (dead code, duplication, or complexity):

1. **Fix the code** — remove dead exports/files, extract shared helpers for clone groups, split or simplify complex functions.
2. **Never suppress** — do not add `// fallow-ignore-next-line complexity`, `// fallow-ignore-file complexity`, `// fallow-ignore-next-line code-duplication`, or HTML equivalents unless the user explicitly approves a verified false positive.
3. **Never relax thresholds** — do not change Fallow CLI flags (`--max-cyclomatic`, `--max-cognitive`, `duplicates.threshold`, etc.) or config to make findings pass.

Fix priority when multiple categories fail: dead code → duplication → complexity.

Other Fallow suppressions (e.g. verified false positives for unused exports) are out of scope here unless the user confirms them.
